Make sure you read that whole page before you download as it has
important information regarding what you need to do. 


 There *was* a discussion a while ago about someone who was trying to
 get it to compile using Cygwin and eventually (after seeing the patches
 he'd have to make to get it to compile 3.3.1 I'd guess) he gave up and
 tried djgpp instead - just have to modify the normal config files like
 you do with linux. 

